# Cloud detail review — 2026-09-16

## Scope and result

The live Study03 authoring level samples SVT density directly; its current blur is
not caused by the final RX 4K channel textures. The material samples
`floor(max(CloudDetailMip, per-cloud DetailMip))`; the global value is 0.
High per-cloud mip values retained after source replacement discard fine density.

To limit GPU risk, only three controls were changed, one at a time:

| Actor | Previous DetailMip | New DetailMip |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| CLOUD_S04_F01_Core | 4.175999 | 3 |
| CLOUD_S04_F02_Lobe | 4.084800 | 3 |
| CLOUD_S04_F03_Edge | 3.940799 | 2 |

Same-camera screenshots show clearer edges and internal detail on the large left
cloud. All 28 actor poses and sources were preserved; other mip values were
unchanged. Live MPC values matched the controls. The Study03 level was saved.

Render target mode 0, view sample cap 256 and shadow view cap 80 were retained.
No bake, high-resolution capture or full-scene mip reduction was performed.
No crash occurred during these bounded captures. This is not a sustained GPU
benchmark or a guarantee against future crashes.

Local evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXDetailQuality_20260916/` contains before/after
screenshots, actor snapshots, map backup and verification output. Final RX baked
textures are unchanged; a later explicit rebake is required to include these edits.

## Follow-up: exterior and internal detail

After the user requested more exterior detail, F01 and F02 were compared at mip 2
using the same camera and unchanged render settings. Both retain more small-scale
structure than mip 3. F01 now uses Density 3.1 and EdgeCut 0.024; F02 uses Density
2.05 and EdgeCut 0.019. These modest density/cut changes reduce weak outer density
and preserve the central mass. No new noise samples or material code were added.

The saved result improves fine edge definition; it does not fully solve broad
lighting flatness or the reconstruction limit of render target mode 0. Actor
poses and source selections, and all values on the other 26 controls, were verified
unchanged against this follow-up's baseline. F03 retains mip 2 from the first pass.
Evidence is in `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXEdgeDetail_20260916/`. No crash occurred in
these captures; sustained GPU stability remains unmeasured.

## Follow-up: internal scattering shade

On `M_VC_CloudAuthoring`, native advanced-volume constants were changed from
multi-scattering contribution 0.60 to 0.45 and occlusion 0.40 to 0.55. Both input
pins were verified unconnected, so the constants are active. Octave count stays
1, eccentricity 0.5 and phase G 0.35. Material compilation passed with no errors.
On the active CloudLayout component, Sky Light Cloud Bottom Occlusion changed
from 0.64 to 0.82. Ray-marched volume shadows remain enabled.

The same-camera result is subtle; broad interior depth is still not strongly
resolved in this lighting/view. Do not describe this pass as a major volumetric
improvement. No phase, density, source, detail, lighting-actor, render-mode or
sample-count change was made in this pass. Current render mode/caps are 0/256/80.
Saved native material dependencies contain no UnrealMCP references. Evidence:
`MCPGameProject/Saved/RXInternalShade_20260916/` (before/after/final images,
settings, backups, compile output in session and verification report).
No GPU crash was observed in the bounded comparison; no sustained benchmark or
rebake was performed.
